{# How to read a table document with the table tools, from the overview to one cell. The
   order follows the tool texts: the overview gives the sheets and the column ids that the
   other tools take. #}
Reading a spreadsheet

A spreadsheet, a CSV file or a table in a document is a table document. Name it by the file_hash and the collection of a search result.

1. Call {{ tool('table_overview') }} first. It lists the sheets and the columns with their ids.
2. Read rows with {{ tool('table_page') }}. One call gives 50 rows. Sort and filter the rows in the call. Give row_start to go to a row of a large sheet, and columns to read the columns after the 60th.
3. Before you filter by a value, call {{ tool('table_column_values') }}. It gives the values of one column and their counts, so you filter by a value that exists.
4. To find a value in a sheet, call {{ tool('table_search_cells') }}. Then read the rows around the match with {{ tool('table_page') }}.
5. When {{ tool('table_page') }} cuts a long cell, read it whole with {{ tool('table_cell') }}. Give the row_id of the row and the column id.

Give the sheet, the row and the column of each value in your answer, so the reader can find it.
